James shared a block of Python code for plotting regulation ranges and state of charge (SOC) using the `plotnine` library. He encountered an error when calling `plot2.show()`, which was related to the `hue_pal()` function in `plotnine`. I suggested several troubleshooting steps, including checking for typos in the DataFrame, inspecting the "Approach" column, updating or reinstalling `plotnine`, and trying a temporary workaround by removing color specifications. I also recommended using `scale_color_manual()` to provide custom colors if issues persisted.
